From 0a1881221b2ce6d3db17c1d92e6d2787941b77ed Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MasherDon <62326358+MasherDon@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 10:00:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 34/91] llama : P1 head yield, on by default
 (LLAMA_HEAD_YIELD=N, default 64, 0 = off) - the output head gets a GPU buffer
 of its own; a decode call of more than N tokens releases it and runs at -ub
 with the head's VRAM in the compute buffers, the graph ends at the normed
 hidden state and the output rows keep it; at the end of a call with outputs
 the compute buffers shrink to N tokens, the CUDA pool gives its peak back
 (new ggml_backend_cuda_trim: cuMemUnmap while nothing is in use, the CUDA
 graphs dropped), the head is read back from its file through the stream's
 handles (~185-206 ms for 1.23 GiB) and a small graph computes the logits -
 bitwise those of the full graph (SiegeLadder runs.md 4.48: 129 of 129 rows at
 4K -ub 512; the 30K consultant at -ub 1024 / 1536 keeps the head on the card:
 decode +18..+28%, prefill unchanged). DeepSeek V4 only, not next to MTP /
 paired / embedding contexts; a call it cannot finish (all outputs, more than
 64, backend samplers) gets the head back first and the full -ub reserve.
 Also: runahead's default K = min(6, n_expert_used) (a K = 5 / 4 model never
 uses a sixth guess, runs.md 4.47); attach_backend's WDDM note and VRAM probe
 only for the GPU backend (the CPU pass printed the note twice and probed 16
 GiB of RAM); LLAMA_HEAD_YIELD_DEBUG=1 prints a hash of every output row's
 logits

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
